                    },
                    "message": "@jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com - Please revert this commit.  @wangmin@phytium.com.cn only has a single one-line commit to the entire openbmc organization.  They are not sufficiently qualified to be listed as a maintainer.\n\nAdding members of the TOF for visibility."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "> @jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com - Please revert this commit.  @wangmin@phytium.com.cn only has a single one-line commit to the entire openbmc organization.  They are not sufficiently qualified to be listed as a maintainer.\n> \n> Adding members of the TOF for visibility.\n@patrick@stwcx.xyz Okay. I\u2019m reverting this commit. However, Min has been actively reviewing code changes in the obmc-ikvm repo, so I believe he is qualified to be added as a reviewer. What do you think?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I'm honestly fine with anyone being a listed reviewer, but I know we have guidelines listed in the document I pointed to.  If you're comfortable with Min being a reviewer, go for it.\n\nMaintainer has a lot more privilege: they can merge code, including their own.  We have to ensure we build up the trust first before we give this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Understood and I agree with your point.\n\nI will encourage Min to continue contributing as a reviewer.\n\nThanks!"
                }
